.Dd April 15, 2019
.Dt ARCHIVE_ENTRY_MISC 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm archive_entry_compression ,
.Nm archive_entry_set_compression ,
.Nm archive_entry_compressed_size ,
.Nm archive_entry_compressed_size_is_set ,
.Nm archive_entry_set_compressed_size ,
.Nm archive_entry_unset_compressed_size ,
.Nm archive_entry_symlink_type ,
.Nm archive_entry_set_symlink_type
.Nd miscellaneous functions for manipulating properties of archive_entry
.Sh LIBRARY
Streaming Archive Library (libarchive, -larchive)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In archive_entry.h
.Ft int
.Fn archive_entry_compression "struct archive_entry *"
.Ft int
.Fn archive_entry_set_compression "struct archive_entry *" "int"
.Ft la_int64_t
.Fn archive_entry_compressed_size "struct archive_entry *"
.Ft int
.Fn archive_entry_compressed_size_is_set "struct archive_entry *"
.Ft void
.Fn archive_entry_set_compressed_size "struct archive_entry *" "la_int64_t"
.Ft void
.Fn archive_entry_unset_compressed_size "struct archive_entry *"
.Ft int
.Fn archive_entry_symlink_type "struct archive_entry *a"
.Ft void
.Fn archive_entry_set_symlink_type "struct archive_entry *a" "int"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The function
.Fn archive_entry_symlink_type
returns and the function
.Fn archive_entry_set_symlink_type
sets the type of the symbolic link stored in an archive entry.
These functions
have special meaning on operating systems that support multiple symbolic link
types (e.g. Microsoft Windows).
.Pp
Supported values are:
.Bl -tag -width "AE_SYMLINK_TYPE_DIRECTORY" -compact
.It AE_SYMLINK_TYPE_UNDEFINED
Symbolic link target type is not defined (default on unix systems)
.It AE_SYMLINK_TYPE_FILE
Symbolic link points to a file
.It AE_SYMLINK_TYPE_DIRECTORY
Symbolic link points to a directory
.El
.Pp
The function
.Fn archive_entry_compression
returns and the function
.Fn archive_entry_set_compression
sets the compression type recorded in an archive entry,
i.e. the method used to store the entry in an archive.
.Fn archive_entry_set_compression
returns
.Dv ARCHIVE_OK
on success, or
.Dv ARCHIVE_FAILED
if
.Fa type
is not one of the recognized values.
The recognized compression types are:
.Bl -tag -width "ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_UNSPECIFIED" -compact
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_UNSPECIFIED
The compression type is not specified.
This is the initial value for a new or cleared object.
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_STORE
Stored without compression.
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_DEFLATE
Compressed using deflate.
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_BZIP2
Compressed using bzip2.
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_LZMA
Compressed using LZMA.
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_LZMA2
Compressed using LZMA2.
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_XZ
Compressed using XZ.
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_ZSTD
Compressed using Zstandard.
.It Dv ARCHIVE_ENTRY_COMPRESSION_PPMD
Compressed using PPMd.
.El
.Pp
The function
.Fn archive_entry_compressed_size
returns the compressed size of the entry, i.e. the number of bytes
its data occupies in the archive, if it has been set, and 0 otherwise.
.Fn archive_entry_compressed_size_is_set
can be used to query that status.
.Fn archive_entry_set_compressed_size
and
.Fn archive_entry_unset_compressed_size
set and unset the compressed size, respectively.
Negative values passed to
.Fn archive_entry_set_compressed_size
are treated as 0.
The compressed size is not calculated by libarchive; it is recorded
only as supplied by the caller or a reader, and is independent of
.Fn archive_entry_size .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr archive_entry 3 ,
.Xr archive_entry_paths 3 ,
.Xr archive_entry_stat 3 ,
.Xr libarchive 3
